### Inspector Permissions

Inspectors can access only their assigned inspection groups and authorized school information.

Group members can:

- Record observations.
- Upload photographs.
- Upload documents.
- Submit individual findings.
- Add timestamps.
- Add inspection notes.

Group leaders can:

- Review member findings.
- Request additional evidence.
- Coordinate tasks.
- Prepare final reports.
- Submit reports to the Super Admin.

### Inspection Workflow

1. Super Admin creates an inspection group.
2. Selects a government or private school.
3. Links relevant complaints.
4. Adds inspectors.
5. Assigns a group leader.
6. Group receives an assignment.
7. Inspectors perform their work.
8. Inspectors submit individual findings.
9. Group leader reviews submissions.
10. Group leader creates the final report.
11. Group leader submits the report.
12. Status becomes REPORT_SUBMITTED.
13. Super Admin reviews the report.
14. Super Admin approves it or requests revisions.
15. Approved inspection becomes COMPLETED.
16. Group status becomes CLOSED.

A submitted report must never automatically close the group.

