# 14. ROLE-BASED DATA ISOLATION

Implement strict RBAC.

SUPER_ADMIN:
- Global platform access.
- All government schools.
- All private schools.
- All users.
- All complaints.
- All inspection groups.
- All reports.
- System settings.

SCHOOL_OWNER:
- Access only to their authorized school or schools.
- Manage their school's academic records.
- View complaints associated with their schools.
- Respond to complaints.
- View their inspection-related notices.
- Cannot access another school's confidential information.

PARENT:
- Access their own account.
- View public school directory.
- Access only approved connected children.
- Submit complaints.
- Track their own complaints.
- Cannot access other parents' information.

STUDENT:
- Access their own academic records.
- View attendance.
- View results.
- View timetable.
- View announcements.

INSPECTOR:
- Access assigned inspection groups only.
- View authorized target school information.
- Submit inspection findings.
- Upload evidence.
- Cannot change school registration or verification.
- Cannot resolve complaints independently.
- Cannot close inspection groups.

GROUP_LEADER:
- All inspector permissions.
- Manage group investigation tasks.
- Review team submissions.
- Submit the final report.

Every protected backend route must validate permissions independently.

Never rely only on hiding frontend buttons.

