# 20. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

1. Government and private schools must use the same platform.

2. Both school categories require registration review.

3. Only approved schools can access operational school management modules.

4. Approved does not automatically mean verified.

5. Government schools are not automatically verified.

6. Private schools are not automatically unverified.

7. The Super Admin controls verification.

8. Parents can register without Super Admin approval.

9. The Super Admin can block parents.

10. Blocked accounts cannot access protected APIs.

11. Parents can complain about both government and private schools.

12. School owners cannot delete parent complaints.

13. Inspectors only access assigned inspection groups.

14. Group leaders submit final inspection reports.

15. The Super Admin must approve final reports before inspection closure.

16. Corrective actions must be tracked independently from complaint status.

17. Every sensitive administrative action must be recorded in audit logs.

18. Student information must only be accessible to authorized users.

19. Ownership type must not determine academic module availability.

20. School suspension must restrict operational access according to administrative policy without deleting historical records.

21. Historical complaints, inspection reports, and audit records must remain available to authorized administrators even when a school is suspended.

22. Multi-campus private school organizations must be supported through a parent organization and separate campus records. Government school hierarchy should also support district and regional administrative structures.

